Third-party data
----------------
The gradient files in assets/gradients/ and the example flames in
testdata/ are taken from the JWildfire distribution.

Taprats (optional, GPL)
-----------------------
The `taprats` variation (crates/rwf-core/src/variations/taprats.rs and
the tilings in assets/taprats/) is ported from Taprats, as included in
JWildfire (package csk.taprats):
Copyright (C) 2000 Craig S. Kaplan, 2010 Pierre Baillargeon
Taprats is licensed under the GNU General Public License, version 3 or
(at your option) any later version. The variation is only compiled with
the cargo feature `taprats`, which is off by default; a build with it is
covered by the GPL version 3 (COPYING) as a whole.

Intel Open Image Denoise (optional)
-----------------------------------
RWildFire can use Intel Open Image Denoise (OIDN), which it loads at
runtime if present; it is not part of the source code. When OIDN is
distributed with RWildFire (tools/fetch_oidn.py), its license (Apache
License 2.0) and third-party notices are placed in oidn-license/ next
to the libraries.
Copyright 2018 Intel Corporation
https://github.com/RenderKit/oidn
